// Servers calling webhook and tunnel services, or downloading from a bare address
// Agentic attack detections by ThreatDefence (general intrusion behavior, first written for ARTEX). Source: https://threatdefence.com/article/artex-agentic-attack-framework-detection-hunting
// ATT&CK: T1105 (Ingress Tool Transfer), T1567.004 (Exfiltration Over Web Service: Exfiltration Over Webhook), T1572 (Protocol Tunneling)
// Example hunt for Microsoft Sentinel and Defender XDR advanced hunting. Test and baseline before alerting.
// Microsoft's own hunt for Storm-3358 follows the same idea: list the addresses curl downloaded from in the last day that it did not use in the week before.

// Example: Defender for Endpoint, curl, wget and netcat talking to collection services or raw IP addresses
DeviceProcessEvents
| where Timestamp > ago(30d)
| where FileName in~ ("curl.exe", "curl", "wget", "nc", "ncat", "nc.exe")
| extend Target = extract(@"(https?://[^\s""']+)", 1, ProcessCommandLine)
| extend RawIP = extract(@"https?://(\d{1,3}(?:\.\d{1,3}){3})", 1, ProcessCommandLine)
| where ProcessCommandLine has_any ("webhook.site", "oast.", "interact.sh", "ngrok", "trycloudflare.com")
    or (isnotempty(RawIP) and not(ipv4_is_private(RawIP)))
    or (FileName in~ ("nc", "ncat", "nc.exe") and ProcessCommandLine has_any (" -e ", " -c "))
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, AccountName, InitiatingProcessFileName, FileName, Target, ProcessCommandLine
| order by Timestamp asc
